course: dictionary
lesson: 4444
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is used. Handwash is one of these words. Read the words around it and ask: what would fit here?
explain: A bottle of handwash on the sink is liquid soap for washing your hands. Here handwash is a noun for the soap itself.
explain: On a clothes label, «handwash only» means the clothes must be washed by hand in water, not in a washing machine. Here handwash is a verb.
explain: Handwashing is the act of washing your hands with soap and water. Health lessons teach that handwashing with soap for about 20 seconds removes germs, which helps stop illness spreading.
fact: Handwash can mean liquid soap for washing your hands.
fact: To handwash clothes means to wash them by hand in water, not in a washing machine.
fact: Handwashing is the noun for washing your hands with soap and water.
fact: «In 1847 Ignaz Semmelweis showed handwashing saved mothers' lives but was mocked» shows that handwashing was not always believed, even when it worked.
fact: «Edward Jenner made the first vaccine in 1796» and «Fleming noticed penicillin in 1928» are other moments in the history of fighting disease.
exercise: «Put a little handwash on your palms and rub them together.» In this sentence, what is handwash? | A towel for drying your face | A cold drink from the tap | A machine that spins wet clothes | *Liquid soap for washing your hands
exercise: The label on Mum's jumper says «handwash only». What does this tell you? | Wash it in a hot machine with bleach | *Wash it by hand in water, not in a washing machine | Dry it on the radiator | Do not wash it at all, put it in the bin
exercise: «Handwashing with soap removes germs from your skin.» What kind of word is handwashing here? | *A noun, the act of washing your hands | A number | A verb meaning to dry | An adjective describing skin
exercise: Nadia says handwash can only mean soap. Is she right? | Yes, it only ever means soap | No, it means a towel | Yes, it means a type of bath | *No, it can also mean washing clothes by hand
test: «In 1847 Ignaz Semmelweis showed handwashing saved mothers' lives but was mocked.» According to this sentence, what did handwashing do? | Was a joke | *Saved mothers' lives | Cost a lot of money | Made mothers sick
test: Grandma says, «I will handwash the lace curtains in a bowl.» What does handwash mean here? | Buy new curtains | *Wash them by hand in water | Hang them outside to dry | Put them in the machine on a fast spin
exam: Bella reads «Some scientists think meeting many harmless germs outdoors trains a child's immune system, but this never means skipping handwashing before eating.» What does the sentence teach? | Handwashing is never needed | Only doctors need to wash their hands | Germs are always bad for you | *Handwashing before eating is still important
